      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We have developed an ambulatory recorder capable of monitoring low back muscle tension, trunk motion, and ratings of pain and fatigue. It weighs 22 ounces, fits into a canteen belt, and records every second for 18 hours. Eleven subjects wore the recorder during all walking hours for between 3 and 5 days. Six subjects had chronic low back pain due to muscle tension, three experienced low back pain after labor, and two had no pain. Movement and muscle tension correlated highly when subjects were pain free but not when they were in pain. Muscle tension increased before pain was experienced."},
